      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The shift to an automated economy is better understood as a dynamic interplay of both technological inevitability and deliberate policy choices. While AI and robotics represent a forward momentum of innovation, the pace of adoption and distribution of benefits often hinge on government regulations and corporate strategies. Ultimately, framing this transition solely as one or the other overlooks how society actively shapes the trajectory of automation.",
